WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.170
The supplied fictional case uses three tabletop tests.

00:00:03.646 --> 00:00:06.118
First, complete intake with a date reaches the

00:00:06.177 --> 00:00:09.776
named reviewer as a draft. Second, intake without

00:00:09.810 --> 00:00:11.807
a date remains pending and asks for the

00:00:11.842 --> 00:00:16.347
missing information. Third, complete intake without approval stays

00:00:16.417 --> 00:00:19.749
unapproved and does not permit delivery. The baseline

00:00:19.795 --> 00:00:23.072
fails the third case. After repairing the gate,

00:00:23.420 --> 00:00:26.427
repeat that case on the revised version. Then

00:00:26.497 --> 00:00:29.190
rerun the ordinary and missing-input cases to check

00:00:29.237 --> 00:00:33.451
for unintended changes. Keep the input, expected behavior,

00:00:33.857 --> 00:00:37.213
observed behavior, result, and version for each test.

00:00:38.107 --> 00:00:41.717
Criteria-based feedback is a comparison with stated criteria.

00:00:42.309 --> 00:00:44.806
Label it accurately; it is not approval by

00:00:44.864 --> 00:00:48.768
a person. These supplied observations are teaching evidence.

00:00:48.989 --> 00:00:51.659
Your completion claim needs your own recorded tests

00:00:51.729 --> 00:00:53.505
and a retested material correction.
